Here is a math problem written in LaTeX: The truncated right circular cone below has a large base radius 8 cm and a small base radius of 4 cm. The height of the truncated cone is 6 cm.  The volume of this solid is $n \pi$ cubic cm, where $n$ is an integer.  What is $n$? [asy]
import olympiad; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); dotfactor=4;
draw(ellipse((0,0),4,1)); draw(ellipse((0,3),2,1/2));
draw((-3.97,.1)--(-1.97,3.1)^^(3.97,.1)--(1.97,3.1));

[/asy]

